ted automatically. The last section opts out of numbering with a `no-number` class.\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<title>Project Update</title>\n<style>\n  body { font-family: Georgia, serif; max-width: 40em; margin: 2em auto; line-height: 1.5; }\n  body { counter-reset: section; }\n  h2::before { counter-increment: section; content: counter(section) \". \"; }\n  h2.no-number::before { content: none; counter-increment: none; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<h1>Project Update</h1>\n\n<h2>Background</h2>\n<p>This project began as a small experiment to streamline our weekly reporting process. Early results were promising enough to justify a wider rollout.</p>\n\n<h2>Progress</h2>\n<p>The core features are complete and have been tested by a pilot group. Feedback has been positive, with only minor usability issues reported.</p>\n\n<h2 class=\"no-number\">Conclusion</h2>\n<p>The project is on track. Remaining work focuses on polish and documentation, and we expect to finish within the next month.</p>\n\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n**How it works**\n- `counter-reset: section` initializes the counter on `body`.\n- Each `<h2>` increments the counter and displays it via `::before`, so adding or reordering sections renumbers them automatically.\n- `h2.no-number` suppresses both the number and the increment, leaving the final \"Conclusion\" section unnumbered.\n\nRendered, it looks like:\n\n> **1. Background**\n> **2. Progress**\n> **Conclusion**\n\nIf you'd prefer this in another format (Word, LaTeX, or Markdown), let me know and I can adapt it. In LaTeX, for example, the last section would use `\\section*{...}`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":577,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":577},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"